  "worked_solution": "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+6}{6}=\\frac{z+11}{2}=t\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+2 \\\\ y=6t-6 \\\\ z=2t-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =121 \\\\ ((2t+2)-2)^{2}+((6t-6)+6)^{2}+(2t-11)^{2} & =121 \\\\ (2t)^{2}+(6t)^{2}+(2t-11)^{2} & =121 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+36{t}^{2}+(4{t}^{2}-44t+121) & =121 \\\\ 44{t}^{2}-44t+121 & =121 \\\\ 44{t}^{2}-44t & =0 \\\\ t(t-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+2=2 \\\\ y=6(0)-6=-6 \\\\ z=2(0)-11=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(2,-6,-11).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)+2=4 \\\\ y=6(1)-6=0 \\\\ z=2(1)-11=-9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(4,0,-9).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(2,-6,-11)$ and $(4,0,-9).$",
